al task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN4-ECB-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Rewrite a muddled ten-line draft into three unified paragraphs with accurate punctuation and two cohesion phrases labelled. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Strong answer: Two or three clear sentences/paragraphs with capitals, stops and a possessive if used; ideas sequenced. Reasoning: I used paragraph unity by attending to topic control rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Comma-splicing whole clauses without a conjunction or stop. Correction: Strong answer: Two or three clear sentences/paragraphs with capitals, stops and a possessive if used; ideas sequenced. Why: the correction restores accurate use of paragraph unity.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Comma-splicing whole clauses without a conjunction or stop. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating paragraph unity on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with paragraph unity, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Strong answer: Two or three clear sentences/paragraphs with capitals, stops and a possessive if used; ideas sequenced. This matches the lesson skill for paragraph unity.","options":["Strong answer: Two or three clear sentences/paragraphs with capitals, stops and 